WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }
::cue(c.credits) { color: #a8c7fa; font-size: 78%; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:04.780
Fight, crash through, and face the challenge!

3
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:08.000
These are our hard knock days.

4
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.830
Can't quench our thirst with a peaceful, everyday life.

5
00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.340
Here we go - don't ever run away!

6
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:19.380
Let's go on living as the mighty winds take us!

7
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.870
We've still got so far to go.

8
00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:26.390
Gotta keep going through the hard knock days.

9
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:31.610
Let's do it again, yes, baby. How many times

10
00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:34.110
do I have to stand back up to make my dream come true?

11
00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.730
Feels like the strength of my resolve

12
00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.200
is put to the test everyday.

13
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.700
Hey, let's go!

14
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:44.450
I don't want to make excuses and settle for being mediocre.

15
00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:45.960
Hey, let's go!

16
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.670
We leapt into a crazy, lawless world.

17
00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:54.170
As I struggled for a foothold, reality caught me off guard.

18
00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:59.470
Even if it beats me, hits me, knocks me down again,

19
00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:00.220
Oh!

20
00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:04.560
Only when we get back on our feet and look forward,

21
00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.450
will we have the last laugh, be the winners!

22
00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:10.120
We gotta go down this glory road, till we reach our goal!

23
00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.720
Fight, shake it off, act strong!

24
00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.720
These are our hard knock days.

25
00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:20.730
There's no such thing as a safe choice.

26
00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.060
Here we go - we'll always be the strongest!

27
00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:27.320
Let's keep moving - never mind the consequences.

28
00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.900
Let's put our wishes all together,

29
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:34.910
and keep on going through the hard knock days.

30
00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:45.830
<b>The Curse of Heart</b>

31
00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:55.470
Has your sword ever broken?

32
00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:57.300
Huh?

33
00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:00.980
Yeah, it's happened a few times, I guess.

34
00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:03.560
Including by you.

35
00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:06.120
Were it clad in Haki,

36
00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:09.150
that same sword would not have shattered.

37
00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:13.400
The slightest nick to your blades is a shame to you.

38
00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.700
Every sword can become a Black Blade.

39
00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:20.160
Until you master it, drinking is forbidden.

40
00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.000
Huh?!

41
00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:30.040
No nicks.

42
00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:43.360
<b>Behind the Former
Royal Plateasu</b>

43
00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.350
Was anyone harmed?

44
00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:46.020
No, sir. It's all thanks to you, Isshou-san.

45
00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:50.240
Because you temporarily levitated those stones, there are no casualties.

46
00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:54.360
Luckily, we already set up downtown as an evacuation zone.

47
00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.200
Well done.

48
00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:00.900
<b>Port town Acacia</b>

49
00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.290
Did you see that?!

50
00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:01.080
That giant statue was sliced completely in half!

51
00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.640
Does that mean the top commander was done in?

52
00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:08.120
<b>Royal Plateau</b>

53
00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:06.800
Pica-sama's down!

54
00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:12.200
He's that strong, and yet he didn't enter the competition?

55
00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.880
What a humble guy.

56
00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:16.420
That power, yet he's merely Garp's grandson's subordinate?

57
00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.230
He's good!

58
00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:24.120
We managed to protect King Riku in the end, so I'll let it go. But still...

59
00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:31.800
The factory...!

60
00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:34.940
The factory that rose from the ground exploded!

61
00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.110
What's going on?!

62
00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:42.120
<b>Inside the
SMILE factory</b>

63
00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.860
One more time!

64
00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:46.560
Yeah!

65
00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.640
Heave-ho!

66
00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:57.850
Blow the factory to bits for making us suffer!

67
00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:00.880
We'll never be fooled or forced to work again!

68
00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:15.100
Hey, hey! Pica has been defeated and the factory just exploded, Doffy.

69
00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:22.710
But the defeated will be brought back. The factory will be restored.

70
00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:24.820
Celebrate while you can!

71
00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:30.540
We still have the Healing Fruit power user, Mansherry, on our side!

72
00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:36.670
Rebecca-sama!

73
00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.730
Robiland!

74
00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:41.100
Are you alright?

75
00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:42.110
<b>The Fourth Level
Outside the Palace
The Sunflower Field</b>

76
00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:50.660
Commander! You're Commander Kyros, right?

77
00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:53.800
Yup! I see you rescued the princess, Leo!

78
00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:57.560
You look so gallant! A spitting image of the statue!

79
00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.510
It's the other way around.

80
00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:05.400
Oh, you're badly injured.
I'll heal you right away.

81
00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.990
Actually, hold on.

82
00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:09.340
You must be Princess Mansherry.

83
00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:14.670
I heard a lot about your power,
but there must be some limit to it.

84
00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:16.120
Don't use it on me.

85
00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.920
But you're bleeding everywhere!

86
00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:23.300
I'm fine. I'm still conscious.

87
00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.470
More importantly, I'm glad that you're okay. It must have been tough.

88
00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:32.180
If you're willing to use your power, there are people all over the country in need of it!

89
00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:35.390
What? This is...

90
00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:55.900
This is Dressrosa?

91
00:05:57.140 --> 00:06:00.060
Leo and the others explained the situation to me,

92
00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:01.920
but I didn't expect it to be this bad...

93
00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:05.700
Still, it looks like they succeeded in destroying the factory.

94
00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:07.590
The battle has come to a crucial point!

95
00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:11.390
This country was entrapped by Doflamingo.

96
00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:15.190
Whether we can return it to the hands of King Riku...

97
00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:18.560
or fall once again and become a land of despair...

98
00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:26.820
Our hope now rests with a certain band of pirates!

99
00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:28.370
Pirates?

100
00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.160
In the royal palace...

101
00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.280
On the top floor...

102
00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:48.600
Luffyland... Lawland...

103
00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:51.050
Those two are our last resort.

104
00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:54.760
Luffy... Traf-kun...

105
00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:57.220
Lucy...

106
00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:17.830
<b>Beneath the Palace
Inside the Outer Wall Tower</b>

107
00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:25.390
I've just entered the rampart tower.

108
00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:29.360
Looks like something bad's about to go down.

109
00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:31.600
Sabo-kun, can't you get here? Where are you?

110
00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:35.050
I'm helping trapped prisoners escape from the Colosseum.

111
00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:37.380
You're too far away.

112
00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:41.960
You can handle pretty much anything on your own, right?

113
00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:45.480
If I thought I could handle this, I wouldn't be calling you! This might affect Luffy-kun!

114
00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:47.630
I'll be right there!

115
00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:48.150
Jeez!

116
00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:53.230
<b>Former Royal Plateau</b>

117
00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.360
Zoro! Do you need a hand?

118
00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:54.910
I'm okay! Ain't a scratch on me!

119
00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:19.250
Zoro, thank you! I thought I was done for!

120
00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:21.730
Zoro-dono, very well done!

121
00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:23.800
Pirate, thank you!

122
00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:27.440
When I saw you cut that giant statue with your swords, I could hardly believe my eyes!

123
00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:31.340
Hold it, you guys!

124
00:08:31.340 --> 00:08:35.780
Hold off on the excitement until that suffocating cage disappears!

125
00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:42.370
It's still there, which means the key man hasn't been defeated yet.

126
00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:53.760
<b>Royal Palace</b>

127
00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:00.250
<b>First Floor</b>

128
00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:15.030
Stop, Bellamy!

129
00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:17.360
Stop!

130
00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:25.790
That bastard isn't worth risking your life for!

131
00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:30.980
That's for me to decide!

132
00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:08.100
Your body's in tatters already...

133
00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:14.180
If you keep fighting, you really will die!

134
00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:26.140
Even if I die, if I can take you down...

135
00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:32.410
Doflamingo might at least remember me a little!

136
00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:00.630
He said he set you free, but...

137
00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:07.220
That's enough, Bellamy. I set you free.

138
00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:10.100
Like you have always been.

139
00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:15.270
...you didn't run, and now you're fighting me to the death...

140
00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:21.680
He must have known you'd do this.

141
00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:27.540
I'm sure he did! But so what?!

142
00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:30.800
I respect him!

143
00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:33.880
If I can at least die in a way that would impress him...

144
00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:36.130
I'll be content!

145
00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:39.600
Don't lie! This is the only option you have left, right?!

146
00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:42.720
Because you're a man!

147
00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:49.990
If you understand that much, shut up and fight!

148
00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:51.440
But you'll die for nothing!

149
00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:58.460
No, this is what I want.

150
00:11:59.640 --> 00:12:03.740
If I'm to meet my end, it should be...

151
00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:07.260
by another man that I admire!

152
00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:15.680
Where are you going, Straw Hat?!

153
00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:17.420
The sky!

154
00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:26.120
What are you saying?! Bellamy has changed!

155
00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:28.000
You've changed, Bellamy.

156
00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:29.480
You're my friend!

157
00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:35.660
Thank you, Straw Hat!

158
00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:40.230
Straw Hat!

159
00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:44.680
If you refuse to fight me...

160
00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:46.950
I'll just...

161
00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:48.910
kill you!

162
00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:55.790
Why're you just standing there?!
Put 'em up, coward!

163
00:12:56.290 --> 00:13:00.860
If you know how to throw a punch, that is!

164
00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:05.440
Die!

165
00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:11.520
So long, Straw Hat!

166
00:13:13.380 --> 00:13:16.520
Thank you for calling me your friend!

167
00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:53.960
I get it now!

168
00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:59.500
That I admired the wrong man!
And how pathetic I am!

169
00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:05.940
I know I'm an idiot...

170
00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:09.480
but even an idiot has principles he must stick to!

171
00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:28.140
Doflamingo!

172
00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:39.190
The beast is roaring.

173
00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:43.260
He should hurry on up here.

174
00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:48.220
I'm sure he'll be surprised, Law...

175
00:14:49.770 --> 00:14:54.970
When he sees your dead body.

176
00:14:58.030 --> 00:15:04.360
<b>A few minutes ago The Royal Palace</b>

177
00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:05.550
Sticky Launcher!

178
00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:17.350
He's still alive.

179
00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:22.980
Hey, hey, hey, Law.
Why don't you just accept defeat already?

180
00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:28.150
You really should rest, Law.

181
00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:37.180
You're not even a match for me on my own.

182
00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:40.000
Why would you want to challenge both of us at the same time?

183
00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:48.920
Straw Hat won't make it up here that easily.

184
00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:53.340
If he had the guts to kill his "friend" right off the bat,

185
00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:56.780
he might have been able to save you, but...

186
00:15:57.590 --> 00:16:01.090
He's such a naive idiot!

187
00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:03.650
Born in the hell that was White Town...

188
00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:09.490
Spending your entire childhood with no hope whatsoever for your future...

189
00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:14.950
But then you met my younger brother, Corazón.

190
00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:18.760
He extended your life expectancy,

191
00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:24.000
and you carried on resenting me, as if you were a ghost of him...

192
00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:29.140
Living only for revenge, what an astounding obsession!

193
00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:30.940
However...

194
00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:33.680
it ends now.

195
00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:38.780
What a waste of thirteen years.

196
00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:40.560
I feel sorry for you.

197
00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:48.330
Your death is inevitable.

198
00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:51.110
You will die a completely meaningless death!

199
00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:54.630
But, if you're going to die anyway...

200
00:16:58.810 --> 00:17:02.020
Wouldn't you rather make something of it?

201
00:17:04.470 --> 00:17:08.170
I have an idea we'd both benefit from.

202
00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:15.510
I'm only going to say this once, so listen carefully,
Trafalgar D. Water Law.

203
00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:25.060
Perform the ultimate Operation Fruit technique on me... the Eternal Youth Operation... and die.

204
00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:32.010
In exchange, I'll grant your wish, whatever it is.

205
00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:33.790
Whatever it is?

206
00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:36.000
If you really mean it...

207
00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:42.370
it's a brilliant idea. We'd both benefit from it.

208
00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:44.910
Alright, I'm in!

209
00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:53.170
You're a very understanding man! Doffy will finally have eternal life!

210
00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:54.720
Then...

211
00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:59.330
Bring Cora-san back to life, right now!

212
00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:04.270
When you're finished doing that,
go lick the asses of everyone in the country!

213
00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:08.720
"No match for" you?
"No use pinning my hopes"?

214
00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:10.770
Don't make me laugh!

215
00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:16.610
You're the one not seeing the whole picture, Doflamingo!

216
00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:23.760
The Straw Hats have caused all sorts of miracles in the past.

217
00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:27.160
You can't beat Straw Hatter!

218
00:18:27.520 --> 00:18:32.090
You won't be able to reclaim Caesar from him, either!

219
00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:38.220
Law, how dare you say that to Doffy!

220
00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:42.760
It's your future that's hanging by a thread-

221
00:18:59.050 --> 00:19:03.470
The letters on your back, "Corazón"?

222
00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:05.930
Are you trying to mock me?

223
00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:09.830
And then there's the name of your crew, the "Heart Pirates"!

224
00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:11.640
Are you trying to mock me?!

225
00:19:13.180 --> 00:19:16.170
You won't even sit on the Seat of Hearts!

226
00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:18.640
So why do you bear the Heart crest?!

227
00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:21.010
Law!

228
00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:30.760
So irritating!

229
00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:42.160
Law, Corazón... This is it.

230
00:19:42.760 --> 00:19:49.160
There's no one left to carry on your ridiculous tenacity!

231
00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:59.380
The curse you've cast on me is broken!

232
00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:01.570
<b>Present time Former Royal Plateau</b>

233
00:20:11.590 --> 00:20:15.610
Straw Hat just took down Bellamy.

234
00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:20.150
That leaves two major enemies in the Donquixote Family.

235
00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:26.900
The only ones left are
the top commander and chief of staff, Trebol,

236
00:20:26.900 --> 00:20:30.330
and the Family boss, Donquixote Doflamingo!

237
00:20:35.070 --> 00:20:36.080
It can't be!

238
00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:38.460
What's the matter, Viola-sama?

239
00:20:43.830 --> 00:20:44.590
Viola?

240
00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:48.120
Our ranks have shrunk as well!

241
00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:53.360
"Our ranks"? You mean out of us was taken out?

242
00:20:53.360 --> 00:20:55.270
Trafalgar Law!

243
00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:23.420
Your majesty?

244
00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:26.510
In a situation where we can't let our guard down at any time,

245
00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:31.600
it's all the more important to keep our people out of harm's way.

246
00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:33.560
Yes, Sir! Let's go!

247
00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:34.520
M-Me, too!

248
00:21:34.950 --> 00:21:36.910
I'll go with you, too!

249
00:21:36.910 --> 00:21:37.650
Me, too!

250
00:21:37.920 --> 00:21:40.660
Alright! Let's go down to the city right now!

251
00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:43.780
It's not too late to minimize casualties!

252
00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:46.780
Yeah! Even though we can't fight, there are still things we can do!

253
00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:48.680
Yeah! Let's go!

254
00:21:54.940 --> 00:21:57.290
Then, all that's left is...

255
00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:03.060
To put an end...

256
00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:06.840
to everything.

257
00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:14.600
Doflamingo!

258
00:22:22.700 --> 00:22:25.150
You're late, Straw Hat.

259
00:22:25.620 --> 00:22:28.440
Now that I've emancipated him,

260
00:22:29.400 --> 00:22:32.240
Bellamy has become "free", right?

261
00:22:32.760 --> 00:22:35.300
Don't play dumb! You knew full well...

262
00:22:43.160 --> 00:22:45.320
that he wasn't gonna run away!

263
00:22:45.520 --> 00:22:47.760
Rubber...

264
00:22:47.960 --> 00:22:49.590
Elephant Gun!

265
00:22:51.220 --> 00:22:52.940
Spiderweb!

266
00:22:57.300 --> 00:23:00.980
I see. So Bellamy didn't run away.

267
00:23:03.680 --> 00:23:05.800
What's so funny?!

268
00:23:11.430 --> 00:23:12.900
Rubber...

269
00:23:13.820 --> 00:23:16.200
Hawk Gatling!

270
00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:35.350
Break White!

271
00:23:40.150 --> 00:23:41.740
That's dangerous!

272
00:23:51.160 --> 00:23:54.860
Hey, Traf!
Why're you bleeding so much?

273
00:23:55.560 --> 00:23:57.060
What happened to your arm?

274
00:23:57.060 --> 00:23:57.800
Hey!

275
00:23:57.800 --> 00:24:00.200
Stay with me, Traf! Hey!

276
00:24:00.750 --> 00:24:02.290
Traf!

277
00:24:07.140 --> 00:24:10.550
He's dead. Obviously.

278
00:24:11.540 --> 00:24:12.590
That's not true!

279
00:24:12.890 --> 00:24:14.560
It is.

280
00:24:14.560 --> 00:24:18.390
He seemed to have a great deal of faith in you, too.

281
00:24:21.240 --> 00:24:27.190
He said you can work miracles.
Can you, Straw Hat?

282
00:24:27.190 --> 00:24:31.080
I didn't think you were that strong
when I fought you, though...

283
00:24:31.900 --> 00:24:34.990
Now, bring it on! There's only two of us left.

284
00:24:34.990 --> 00:24:37.990
How dare you bastards!

285
00:24:53.400 --> 00:24:55.680
Wait! Stay where you are!

286
00:25:07.860 --> 00:25:09.060
No way...

287
00:25:09.060 --> 00:25:10.460
The wall of strings...

288
00:25:14.140 --> 00:25:16.650
is shrinking!

289
00:25:22.280 --> 00:25:25.210
I'll have you follow Law in death shortly.

290
00:25:28.520 --> 00:25:31.460
Let's end this game, shall we?

291
00:25:31.900 --> 00:25:33.840
Mingo!

292
00:25:34.100 --> 00:25:34.800
Wait.

293
00:25:35.860 --> 00:25:38.480
Listen carefully, Straw Hatter.

294
00:25:49.540 --> 00:25:50.770
Look!

295
00:26:05.060 --> 00:26:06.460
It really is moving.

296
00:26:12.260 --> 00:26:14.220
The string wall's moving!

297
00:26:14.710 --> 00:26:16.650
Run for it!

298
00:26:24.560 --> 00:26:27.360
Not even the outskirts of town are safe!

299
00:26:28.970 --> 00:26:31.060
Hurry up and make a break for it!

300
00:26:33.110 --> 00:26:34.570
Get to downtown!

301
00:26:38.820 --> 00:26:40.700
It's the same in the west!

302
00:26:42.580 --> 00:26:44.700
Reporting in! Eastern district, Carta!

303
00:26:44.960 --> 00:26:47.540
Per other reports, the bird cage appears to be shrinking!

304
00:26:54.180 --> 00:26:57.260
The islanders are all headed toward downtown!

305
00:26:57.280 --> 00:27:01.240
<b>The Royal Palace</b>

306
00:26:59.160 --> 00:27:01.220
Sooner or later...

307
00:27:02.960 --> 00:27:05.180
everyone dies, correct?

308
00:27:08.520 --> 00:27:11.820
Straw Hat, haven't you noticed?

309
00:27:11.820 --> 00:27:14.190
The rules of the game have changed.

310
00:27:14.190 --> 00:27:16.540
Game? What are you on about now?!

311
00:27:20.180 --> 00:27:21.920
Just listen.

312
00:27:23.690 --> 00:27:29.290
The bird cage that surrounds this town is shrinking, bit by bit.

313
00:27:32.340 --> 00:27:36.420
It's like an umbrella, slowly closing.

314
00:27:38.630 --> 00:27:42.220
It'll shred apart everything in this country.

315
00:27:43.380 --> 00:27:44.970
In about...

316
00:27:45.360 --> 00:27:48.640
an hour, give or take.

317
00:27:53.560 --> 00:27:57.690
There's nowhere to run.

318
00:27:59.360 --> 00:28:03.050
Save the people on the outskirts of the country, on the double!

319
00:28:03.050 --> 00:28:03.660
Aye!

320
00:28:09.690 --> 00:28:13.780
The weaker citizens have been evacuated
to the edges of the city, so hurry and get them!

321
00:28:14.570 --> 00:28:16.940
Run to the center part of town!

322
00:28:16.940 --> 00:28:18.670
Run! Here come the strings!

323
00:28:20.740 --> 00:28:23.240
Hey! Somebody, help me!

324
00:28:23.240 --> 00:28:25.300
Just freeing my legs would work!

325
00:28:25.300 --> 00:28:28.390
Untie me! I don't wanna die!

326
00:28:29.260 --> 00:28:32.100
T-T-The bird cage is shrinking?!

327
00:28:34.080 --> 00:28:37.790
<b>Former Royal Grounds</b>

328
00:28:34.640 --> 00:28:38.020
What's going on?! The bird cage... The bird cage...

329
00:28:35.520 --> 00:28:37.270
Is this truly happening?

330
00:28:37.270 --> 00:28:38.140
My word...

331
00:28:38.140 --> 00:28:41.160
What do we do?! What can we do?!

332
00:28:41.160 --> 00:28:42.850
Hey, Zoro!

333
00:28:42.850 --> 00:28:47.950
The cage is heading toward us! What's gonna happen to us?!

334
00:28:50.740 --> 00:28:55.540
We finally busted out from behind bars, only to be put behind them again?

335
00:28:55.540 --> 00:28:58.250
Where are we supposed to run?!

336
00:28:58.710 --> 00:29:00.780
How can he stoop so low?

337
00:29:00.780 --> 00:29:04.050
Are you not yet satisfied, Doflamingo?

338
00:29:04.050 --> 00:29:06.470
If the cage keeps shrinking like this...

339
00:29:08.020 --> 00:29:10.270
That's it for Dressrosa!

340
00:29:10.490 --> 00:29:14.290
<b>The Royal Palace Grounds - Second Level</b>

341
00:29:15.280 --> 00:29:18.350
What's all that smoke and rumbling?

342
00:29:18.350 --> 00:29:20.320
What in the world's going on?!

343
00:29:20.320 --> 00:29:25.700
Luffy, hurry up! Kick Doflamingo's ass already!

344
00:29:25.700 --> 00:29:28.910
You're our last hope!

345
00:29:26.620 --> 00:29:29.630
That is right! Indeed! Certainly!

346
00:29:29.630 --> 00:29:34.710
But that is too much to ask. The lives of everyone are in Luffy-dono's hands.

347
00:29:36.300 --> 00:29:39.770
We are counting on you, Luffy-dono!

348
00:29:39.770 --> 00:29:42.380
I am counting on you, too!

349
00:29:47.620 --> 00:29:50.560
I'm not planning on sparing anyone.

350
00:29:55.560 --> 00:30:02.610
What advantage would I gain in allowing people
that have learned this country's secrets survive?

351
00:30:10.540 --> 00:30:13.870
Towns, people, animals...

352
00:30:15.110 --> 00:30:17.760
Even your allies...

353
00:30:18.670 --> 00:30:22.090
And you! Everyone dies!

354
00:30:30.510 --> 00:30:37.810
In other words, your friends just died
a little earlier than they otherwise would have.

355
00:30:39.980 --> 00:30:42.540
Right, Straw Hatter?

356
00:30:42.540 --> 00:30:44.880
Isn't that what he used to call you?

357
00:30:52.080 --> 00:30:55.410
Oh, you needn't worry.

358
00:30:55.410 --> 00:30:57.040
I'll build another country.

359
00:30:57.820 --> 00:31:02.450
Mingo, all I have to do to fix this
is kick your ass!

360
00:31:02.450 --> 00:31:06.460
I've been trying to tell you, you can't do that.

361
00:31:06.460 --> 00:31:08.270
You never learn!

362
00:31:08.270 --> 00:31:09.240
Bullet String!

363
00:31:11.720 --> 00:31:14.100
Rubber...

364
00:31:14.100 --> 00:31:16.640
Join Law in death!

365
00:31:18.040 --> 00:31:18.890
Chambres!

366
00:31:23.400 --> 00:31:24.690
Law!

367
00:31:26.280 --> 00:31:29.400
You're the one that's going to perish, Doflamingo!

368
00:31:30.540 --> 00:31:31.410
Do it!

369
00:31:40.080 --> 00:31:45.040
This operation will destroy you from the inside out!

370
00:31:49.280 --> 00:31:50.760
Gamma Knife!

371
00:32:02.940 --> 00:32:03.860
Doffy!

372
00:32:08.980 --> 00:32:12.660
Law! How are you still alive?!

373
00:32:12.660 --> 00:32:16.080
How are you using your Operation abilities without creating a Room?!

374
00:32:16.480 --> 00:32:18.460
No, this is a Room!

375
00:32:20.280 --> 00:32:26.800
It's at the cost of some of my lifespan,
but I created a Room so big you can't even see it!

376
00:32:28.080 --> 00:32:28.800
What?!

377
00:32:31.630 --> 00:32:35.740
I did it all for this moment... to set up this attack!

378
00:32:55.650 --> 00:32:57.220
He missed my vital organs!

379
00:32:58.120 --> 00:32:59.400
Chambres!

380
00:33:09.860 --> 00:33:11.860
Mingo!

381
00:33:12.080 --> 00:33:12.760
Wait.

382
00:33:15.640 --> 00:33:17.180
I'm alive.

383
00:33:18.480 --> 00:33:20.640
Listen carefully, Straw Hatter.

384
00:33:21.940 --> 00:33:24.460
Don't turn around. I have a plan.

385
00:33:28.580 --> 00:33:31.400
Nobody can defend against an attack from inside their body!

386
00:33:35.200 --> 00:33:38.290
Even you can't counteract this technique!

387
00:33:54.900 --> 00:33:59.850
Doffy, you're a king! Don't prostrate yourself!

388
00:34:05.120 --> 00:34:07.140
Now you've really done it!

389
00:34:08.320 --> 00:34:09.830
It's no use!

390
00:34:09.830 --> 00:34:12.320
Even if you kill me, it's too late for you!

391
00:34:17.320 --> 00:34:20.530
I won't let you live...

392
00:34:22.040 --> 00:34:23.490
Law!

393
00:34:24.480 --> 00:34:26.120
Rubber...

394
00:34:28.100 --> 00:34:31.130
Jet Stamp!

395
00:34:36.100 --> 00:34:37.800
Doffy!

396
00:34:43.640 --> 00:34:46.810
Doffy! Are you alright?

397
00:34:50.080 --> 00:34:51.170
You bastard!

398
00:34:51.170 --> 00:34:53.340
Wait, Straw Hatter!

399
00:35:00.900 --> 00:35:01.660
Traf...

400
00:35:04.760 --> 00:35:09.120
That bastard... is mine!

401
00:35:34.220 --> 00:35:35.480
Room!

402
00:35:42.620 --> 00:35:46.450
You're finished, Doflamingo!

403
00:35:48.420 --> 00:35:50.040
Law!

404
00:35:50.300 --> 00:35:55.840
Damn you! What have you done to Doffy?!

405
00:36:04.220 --> 00:36:05.560
Don't get in his way!

406
00:36:16.220 --> 00:36:17.020
You just...

407
00:36:19.320 --> 00:36:24.960
gathered people that were convenient to you
and called it a "family".

408
00:36:26.680 --> 00:36:33.840
And when your real brother, Cora-san, tried to end your rampage, you...

409
00:36:35.020 --> 00:36:37.400
He's free!

410
00:36:48.600 --> 00:36:52.890
Yeah, that was a shame...

411
00:36:53.400 --> 00:36:59.560
He betrayed me... even pointed a gun at me...

412
00:36:59.560 --> 00:37:00.610
But you knew!

413
00:37:02.040 --> 00:37:05.280
You knew Cora-san couldn't pull the trigger!

414
00:37:10.980 --> 00:37:12.600
I would have pulled it.

415
00:37:20.720 --> 00:37:22.090
I bet you would have.

416
00:37:27.220 --> 00:37:31.060
You're the same as me.

417
00:37:31.720 --> 00:37:34.460
I wanna destroy everything before my eyes!

418
00:37:35.320 --> 00:37:39.780
Towns, houses, people... I wanna destroy them all!

419
00:37:42.740 --> 00:37:46.740
Yeah... That's fine by me.

420
00:37:49.280 --> 00:37:50.740
But on that day...

421
00:37:56.440 --> 00:37:58.960
You should have died, not him!

422
00:38:02.140 --> 00:38:07.460
Law, I'm sure you'll love to hear this...

423
00:38:08.340 --> 00:38:13.970
Corazón was a drag and an eyesore to me.

424
00:38:14.330 --> 00:38:19.770
He acquired this silly sense of justice
and wore that worthless heart of his on his sleeve.

425
00:38:19.920 --> 00:38:21.730
He was an incompetent man.

426
00:38:22.030 --> 00:38:25.320
When I killed him that day,
it was a huge load off my-

427
00:38:25.960 --> 00:38:27.530
Counter Shock!

428
00:38:31.560 --> 00:38:35.330
Go to hell you demonic bastard!

429
00:38:37.480 --> 00:38:39.630
Doffy!

430
00:39:30.500 --> 00:39:34.280
As expected of our king!

431
00:39:38.560 --> 00:39:41.020
H-How the hell...

432
00:39:44.610 --> 00:39:50.410
Given enough time, I can mend myself.

433
00:39:51.350 --> 00:39:57.650
As we speak, the strings within my body are repairing my internal organs.

434
00:39:57.650 --> 00:39:58.760
What?!

435
00:39:58.760 --> 00:40:00.940
It's all about how you use your ability.

436
00:40:02.460 --> 00:40:05.630
It's a bit different from recovery, though.

437
00:40:06.900 --> 00:40:09.050
Good job on the suicide attack.

438
00:40:13.490 --> 00:40:15.970
Sticky Chain!

439
00:40:18.880 --> 00:40:20.850
Stop!

440
00:40:21.150 --> 00:40:23.110
Sticky Stick!

441
00:40:34.120 --> 00:40:37.320
I'll put you out of your misery. It's the least I can do.

442
00:40:44.120 --> 00:40:46.750
Dammit!

443
00:40:52.400 --> 00:40:53.880
Dammit...
